=base:main-content.cmark

# Changelog: tramaj-react

Release history of `tramaj-react`, the React host: folds a tramaj-js Node into React elements. Releases happen when there are
major changes rather than on a schedule; each entry below is one version.
Every implementation has its own page like this one, and each page is
tagged so the site builds one Atom feed per implementation:
#changelog #javascript #tramaj-react

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@version=import("changelog/version", {"package": "tramaj-react"})
.div(class: "changelog",
  $version({
      "version": "0.1.0",
      "date": "unreleased",
      "summary": "The React counterpart of tramaj-halogen, and the only package here that depends on react.",
      "changes": [
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "\`foldToReact\` and \`validateAttrNames\`."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking: \`renderScalar\` renders a number by its type, as \`str\` writes it: an integer as its digits, a float always with a fraction or an exponent. A whole-valued float, which \`tramaj-js\` hands over as a \`Float\`, renders as \`3.0\`."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "A term \`{\"$term\": op, \"arguments\": [...]}\` renders as the call that built it, such as \`sum(#ctx.n, 1.0)\`, and in \`<code>\` in text position like a symbol; \`termLabel\` is exported."
          }
      ]
  }).rendered)

